module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedVarieties.NoDeformations.StalkEssentialFinitePresentation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedVarieties.Support.KoszulDeformation
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Flat
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType

/-!
# The deformation situation at the stalk map of a flat finite-type morphism

`AlgebraicGeometry.FlatLocalKoszulDeformationSituation` has no constructor anywhere in the
library: every result about it takes it as a hypothesis. This file supplies the one geometric
source of such a situation that [Stacks, Tag 0G0R] uses, namely the stalk map

`𝒪_{Y,f(x)} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x}`

of a flat morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` locally of finite type over a locally Noetherian base — in
[Stacks, Tag 0G0R] the projection `X ×_S Y ⟶ S` at a point `z` over `s`. The ring-theoretic
hypotheses of the situation are all automatic for such a stalk map; the Koszul data on the closed
fibre is not, and is taken as an argument.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.flatLocalKoszulDeformationSituationOfStalkMap`: the deformation situation at
  the stalk map of a flat morphism locally of finite type over a locally Noetherian base, given a
  regular sequence on the closed fibre and a perfect complex whose derived restriction to the
  closed fibre is its Koszul complex.

## Implementation notes

*What is discharged here, and what is not.* Of the fields of the situation, the local rings, the
algebra structure, the locality of the algebra map, the flatness and the essential finite
presentation are supplied:

* the stalks of a scheme are local rings, and the two stalk rings of a morphism are related by
  Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.stalkMap`, which is a local homomorphism;
* flatness of the stalk map is flatness of `f`, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Flat.iff_flat_stalkMap`,
  and `RingHom.Flat` is by definition `Module.Flat` for the algebra structure the stalk map
  induces;
* essential finite presentation is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType.isEssentiallyOfFinitePresentation_stalkMap`.

The remaining fields — the length `r`, the sequence on the closed fibre with its membership and
regularity, and the perfect complex with its closed-fibre Koszul identification — are arguments.
They are the geometric input: in [Stacks, Tag 0G0R] they come from the fibre
`(X ×_S Y)_s = Y_s ×_k Y_s` and the local structure of the diagonal of the smooth fibre `Y_s`
there, which this file does not touch.

*Why the arguments are phrased with `(f.stalkMap x).hom` rather than `algebraMap`.* The algebra
structure used is `RingHom.toAlgebra` of the stalk map, whose `algebraMap` is that stalk map by
definition, so the two spellings are interchangeable and the caller never has to produce the
algebra instance in order to state the sequence it is handing over.

No `stacks` attribute is carried: this is the plumbing that lets [Stacks, Tag 0G0N] be applied at
a stalk map, not a result of the source.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G0N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G0N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G0R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G0R)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
  [Flat f] (x : X)

/-- The ideal `𝔪_{Y,f(x)} 𝒪_{X,x}` generated by the maximal ideal of the base in the stalk of the
source: the ideal whose quotient is the local ring of the closed fibre. -/
public abbrev stalkMapFibreIdeal : Ideal (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
  Ideal.map (f.stalkMap x).hom (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (f x)))

/-- **The flat local Koszul deformation situation at a stalk map.** For a flat morphism
`f : X ⟶ Y` locally of finite type over a locally Noetherian base and a point `x : X`, the stalk
map `𝒪_{Y,f(x)} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x}` is a flat local homomorphism of local rings essentially of finite
presentation; together with a regular sequence of length `r` in the local ring
`𝒪_{X,x} / 𝔪_{Y,f(x)} 𝒪_{X,x}` of the closed fibre, and a perfect complex over `𝒪_{X,x}` whose
derived restriction to the closed fibre is the Koszul complex of that sequence, it is a
`AlgebraicGeometry.FlatLocalKoszulDeformationSituation`.

This is the situation [Stacks, Tag 0G0R] applies [Stacks, Tag 0G0N] to, at the projection
`X ×_S Y ⟶ S` and a closed point `z` of the fibre. -/
public def flatLocalKoszulDeformationSituationOfStalkMap
    (r : ℕ)
    (residueSequence : Fin r → (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ stalkMapFibreIdeal f x))
    (residueSequence_mem : ∀ i, residueSequence i ∈
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)).map
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (stalkMapFibreIdeal f x)))
    (residueSequence_regular : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
      (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ stalkMapFibreIdeal f x) (List.ofFn residueSequence))
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} (X.presheaf.stalk x)))
    (K_perfect : StacksDraft.Perfect.IsPerfect K)
    (closedFiber_isKoszul : Nonempty
      ((CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (stalkMapFibreIdeal f x))).functor.obj K ≅
        DerivedCategory.Q.obj
          ((Koszul.seqComplex residueSequence).extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat))) :
    FlatLocalKoszulDeformationSituation.{u} where
  R := Y.presheaf.stalk (f x)
  A := X.presheaf.stalk x
  algebra := (f.stalkMap x).hom.toAlgebra
  localHom := inferInstanceAs (IsLocalHom (f.stalkMap x).hom)
  flat := (Flat.iff_flat_stalkMap f).mp inferInstance x
  essentiallyOfFinitePresentation :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isEssentiallyOfFinitePresentation_stalkMap f x
  r := r
  residueSequence := residueSequence
  residueSequence_mem := residueSequence_mem
  residueSequence_regular := residueSequence_regular
  K := K
  K_perfect := K_perfect
  closedFiber_isKoszul := closedFiber_isKoszul

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
